## 4. Error Handling

| Situation | What the user sees (`error`) |
|---|---|
| Empty input | "Please enter a GitHub repository URL." |
| Wrong site | "The link must be a github.com repository URL." |
| Bad format | "The URL must look like https://github.com/owner/repo." |
| Repo doesn't exist or is private | "Repository not found. … Private repositories cannot be scanned." |
| Rate limit (HTTP 403/429) | "GitHub rate limit reached. Wait about an hour, or set the GITHUB_TOKEN variable." |
| No internet | "Could not reach GitHub. Check your internet connection." |
| Timeout | "GitHub took too long to respond. Please try again." |
| Empty repo (HTTP 409) | "This repository is empty (it has no files yet)." |
| Anything unexpected | "Something unexpected went wrong. Please try again." |

No case shows a raw traceback, and the dictionary keeps its full shape every time.

