## 5. Optimisations Compared with a Typical First Version

| Naive version | This version | Why it is better |
|---|---|---|
| Browses folders one by one | One `recursive=1` tree call | Fewer requests, so less risk of hitting rate limits |
| New connection per request | One `Session` | Faster and more efficient |
| Validates the URL after calling GitHub | Validates first | Bad input never uses the network |
| Hard-coded token | Optional `GITHUB_TOKEN` environment variable | Keeps secrets out of the code |
| Crashes on unexpected errors | Safety net with logging | The app keeps running |
| Variable return shape | `_empty_result()` template | B and C can rely on the same keys every time |
| Repeated checks | Small reusable helpers | Easier to read, test, and change |

