## 6. How to Run and Test

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python repository_analyzer.py       # manual test with real and bad URLs
pytest test_repository_analyzer.py  # offline unit tests
```

Use these checks from the team's test checklist:

- [ ] A valid public repo (e.g. `https://github.com/psf/requests`) returns the correct types for every key.
- [ ] A bad URL and a missing repo show readable errors, not tracebacks.
- [ ] A sparse repo or one with no README still returns predictable data.
- [ ] Turning off Wi-Fi does not crash the app (you get a network error message).

